(window.DSA_TOPIC=window.DSA_TOPIC||{})["trees"]={"id":"trees","theory":"\n<h3>What it is</h3>\n<p>A <b>binary tree</b> is a node with up to two children, <code>left</code> and <code>right</code>, each itself a binary tree. Almost every tree problem is solved by asking: <i>if I already knew the answer for my left and right subtrees, how would I combine them?</i></p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">class TreeNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, left=None, right=None):\n        self.val, self.left, self.right = val, left, right</code></pre>\n<p>A <b>binary search tree (BST)</b> adds a rule: everything in the left subtree is smaller than the node, everything in the right is larger. So an inorder walk gives sorted order, and search takes O(h) where h is the height (log n if balanced, n if it degenerates into a line).</p>\n<h3>Traversals</h3>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Order</th><th>Visit</th><th>Used for</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Preorder</td><td>node, left, right</td><td>copying / serialising a tree, path from root</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Inorder</td><td>left, node, right</td><td>BST → sorted order, k-th smallest, validate BST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Postorder</td><td>left, right, node</td><td>heights, diameters, anything that needs children first</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Level order (BFS)</td><td>row by row with a queue</td><td>levels, right side view, min depth, zigzag</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Spot the pattern</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Height / depth / diameter / balanced / max path\" → postorder DFS that <b>returns</b> one value and updates a global best.</li>\n<li>\"Per level\" → BFS with <code>for _ in range(len(queue))</code>.</li>\n<li>\"Root-to-node path\" or \"carry info downward\" (max so far, bounds) → pass it as a parameter.</li>\n<li>BST + \"find / k-th / validate / LCA\" → use the ordering to go left or right only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Template: postorder that returns height</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">def height(node):\n    if not node:\n        return 0\n    l, r = height(node.left), height(node.right)\n    # combine here: update a global answer with l, r\n    return 1 + max(l, r)</code></pre>\n<h3>Common mistakes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Validating a BST only against the direct parent instead of the full (low, high) range.</li>\n<li>Forgetting the <code>None</code> base case.</li>\n<li>Deep recursion on skewed trees: Python's default limit is 1000 frames — use an explicit stack if n can be large.</li>\n</ul>\n","qs":{"binary-tree-inorder-traversal":{"statement":"Return the inorder traversal (left, node, right) of a binary tree.","examples":[["root = [1, None, 2, 3]","[1, 3, 2]"],["root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, 8, None, None, 6, 7, 9]","[4, 2, 6, 5, 7, 1, 3, 9, 8]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [4, 2, 6, 1, 3, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Recursive DFS: visit left, record the node, visit right.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h) call stack","code":"def inorder_traversal(root):\n    res = []\n\n    def dfs(node):\n        if node:\n            dfs(node.left)\n            res.append(node.val)\n            dfs(node.right)\n    dfs(root)\n    return res"},"opt":{"idea":"Same order with an explicit stack: push the whole left spine, pop and record, then move to the right child. (Morris traversal reaches O(1) space.)","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def inorder_traversal(root):\n    res, stack, cur = [], [], root\n    while cur or stack:\n        while cur:\n            stack.append(cur)\n            cur = cur.left\n        cur = stack.pop()\n        res.append(cur.val)\n        cur = cur.right\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Pop 1 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[2],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["4","2"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 2 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2,1],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["4"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 3 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[2,1,3],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["4"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 4 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[2,1,3,0],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":[],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 5 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[2,1,3,0,5],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":["6"],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pop 6 and record it, then go right","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[2,1,3,0,5,4],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":[],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["2",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1],["6",5,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[2,1,3,0,5,4],"p":{}},{"k":"stack","n":"stack","v":[],"hl":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"res","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"maximum-depth-of-binary-tree":{"statement":"Return the number of nodes on the longest root-to-leaf path.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","3"],["root = [1, None, 2]","2"],["root = []","0"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","brute":{"idea":"List every root-to-leaf path and take the longest.","tc":"O(n · h)","sc":"O(n · h)","code":"def max_depth(root):\n    paths = []\n\n    def walk(node, path):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        path = path + [node.val]\n        if not node.left and not node.right:\n            paths.append(path)\n        walk(node.left, path)\n        walk(node.right, path)\n    walk(root, [])\n    return max((len(p) for p in paths), default=0)"},"opt":{"idea":"depth(node) = 1 + max(depth(left), depth(right)); an empty tree has depth 0.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def max_depth(root):\n    def depth(node):\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        d = 1 + max(depth(node.left), depth(node.right))\n        return d\n    return depth(root)","frames":[{"m":"depth(9) = 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(15) = 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(7) = 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(20) = 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"depth(3) = 3","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"invert-binary-tree":{"statement":"Mirror a binary tree: swap every node's left and right children.","examples":[["root = [4, 2, 7, 1, 3, 6, 9]","[4, 7, 2, 9, 6, 3, 1]"],["root = [2, 1, 3]","[2, 3, 1]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [4, 2, 7, 1, 3, 6, 9]","brute":{"idea":"Build a brand-new mirrored copy of the tree.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n) new nodes","code":"def invert_tree(root):\n    if not root:\n        return None\n    return TreeNode(root.val, invert_tree(root.right), invert_tree(root.left))"},"opt":{"idea":"At every node swap left and right, then invert both subtrees in place.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def invert_tree(root):\n    top = root\n\n    def inv(node):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        node.left, node.right = node.right, node.left\n        inv(node.left)\n        inv(node.right)\n    inv(root)\n    return root","frames":[{"m":"Swap the children of 4","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 7","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 9","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 6","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 2","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 3","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Swap the children of 1","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: [4, 7, 2, 9, 6, 3, 1]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["4",1,4],["7",2,3],["9",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["3",-1,-1],["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"same-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if two binary trees have the same shape and values.","examples":[["p = [1, 2, 3], q = [1, 2, 3]","True"],["p = [1, 2], q = [1, None, 2]","False"],["p = [1, 2, 1], q = [1, 1, 2]","False"]],"vizIn":"p = [1, 2, 3, 4], q = [1, 2, 3, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Serialise both trees with None markers and compare the strings.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def is_same_tree(p, q):\n    def ser(n):\n        return \"#\" if not n else f\"({n.val},{ser(n.left)},{ser(n.right)})\"\n    return ser(p) == ser(q)"},"opt":{"idea":"Recurse on both trees together: both empty → True; one empty or values differ → False; else compare left with left and right with right.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_same_tree(p, q):\n    rp, rq = p, q\n\n    def same(a, b):\n        if not a and not b:\n            return True\n        if not a or not b or a.val != b.val:\n            return False\n        return same(a.left, b.left) and same(a.right, b.right)\n    return same(p, q)","frames":[{"m":"Both 1 — compare children","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Both 2 — compare children","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Mismatch: 4 vs 5","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: False","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"p","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"q","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"symmetric-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if the tree is a mirror of itself around its centre.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 3]","True"],["root = [1, 2, 2, None, 3, None, 3]","False"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 3]","brute":{"idea":"Make an inverted copy and check it equals the original.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def is_symmetric(root):\n    def mirror(n):\n        return None if not n else TreeNode(n.val, mirror(n.right), mirror(n.left))\n\n    def same(a, b):\n        if not a or not b:\n            return a is b\n        return a.val == b.val and same(a.left, b.left) and same(a.right, b.right)\n    return same(root, mirror(root))"},"opt":{"idea":"Compare the left subtree with the right subtree mirrored: outer pair (a.left, b.right) and inner pair (a.right, b.left).","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_symmetric(root):\n    def mirror(a, b):\n        if not a or not b:\n            return a is b\n        return a.val == b.val and mirror(a.left, b.right) and mirror(a.right, b.left)\n    return mirror(root.left, root.right)","frames":[{"m":"Compare 2 with its mirror 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1,4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Compare 3 with its mirror 3","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2,6],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Compare 4 with its mirror 4","l":4,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["2",5,6],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":2},"binary-tree-level-order-traversal":{"statement":"Return the node values level by level, left to right.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","[[3], [9, 20], [15, 7]]"],["root = [1]","[[1]]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Find the height, then for each depth d run a DFS that collects nodes at depth d.","tc":"O(n · h)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def level_order(root):\n    def height(n):\n        return 0 if not n else 1 + max(height(n.left), height(n.right))\n\n    def collect(n, d, out):\n        if not n:\n            return\n        if d == 0:\n            out.append(n.val)\n        collect(n.left, d - 1, out)\n        collect(n.right, d - 1, out)\n    res = []\n    for d in range(height(root)):\n        row = []\n        collect(root, d, row)\n        res.append(row)\n    return res"},"opt":{"idea":"BFS with a queue; process exactly len(queue) nodes per round — that's one level.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(w) — widest level","code":"def level_order(root):\n    from collections import deque\n    if not root:\n        return []\n    res, q = [], deque([root])\n    while q:\n        level = []\n        for _ in range(len(q)):\n            node = q.popleft()\n            level.append(node.val)\n            if node.left:\n                q.append(node.left)\n            if node.right:\n                q.append(node.right)\n        res.append(level)\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Level 0: [3]","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":["9","20"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 1: [9, 20]","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[1,2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":["15","7"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3],[9,20]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 2: [15, 7]","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3],[9,20],[15,7]]"]]}]},{"m":"Result: [[3], [9, 20], [15, 7]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue (next level)","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[3],[9,20],[15,7]]"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"diameter-of-binary-tree":{"statement":"Return the number of edges on the longest path between any two nodes.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","3"],["root = [1, 2]","1"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, None, 6, None, None, 7]","brute":{"idea":"For every node, compute left and right heights with separate calls.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def diameter_of_binary_tree(root):\n    def height(n):\n        return 0 if not n else 1 + max(height(n.left), height(n.right))\n\n    def best(n):\n        if not n:\n            return 0\n        return max(height(n.left) + height(n.right), best(n.left), best(n.right))\n    return best(root)"},"opt":{"idea":"One postorder pass: each node returns its height, and left + right height through it is a candidate diameter.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def diameter_of_binary_tree(root):\n    best = 0\n\n    def height(node):\n        nonlocal best\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        l, r = height(node.left), height(node.right)\n        best = max(best, l + r)\n        return 1 + max(l, r)\n\n    height(root)\n    return best","frames":[{"m":"At 6: left height 0 + right height 0 = 0","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","0"]]}]},{"m":"At 4: left height 1 + right height 0 = 1","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","1"]]}]},{"m":"At 7: left height 0 + right height 0 = 0","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","1"]]}]},{"m":"At 5: left height 0 + right height 1 = 1","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","1"]]}]},{"m":"At 2: left height 2 + right height 2 = 4","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]},{"m":"At 3: left height 0 + right height 0 = 0","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]},{"m":"At 1: left height 3 + right height 1 = 4","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,6],["2",2,4],["4",3,-1],["6",-1,-1],["5",-1,5],["7",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","4"]]}]}]},"tests":2},"balanced-binary-tree":{"statement":"A tree is height-balanced if every node's subtrees differ in height by at most 1. Check it.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","True"],["root = [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, None, None, 4, 4]","False"],["root = []","True"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","brute":{"idea":"At every node compare the heights of both subtrees, computing heights from scratch.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_balanced(root):\n    def height(n):\n        return 0 if not n else 1 + max(height(n.left), height(n.right))\n    if not root:\n        return True\n    return abs(height(root.left) - height(root.right)) <= 1 and is_balanced(root.left) and is_balanced(root.right)"},"opt":{"idea":"Return the height bottom-up, or −1 as soon as any subtree is unbalanced — the −1 short-circuits upward.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_balanced(root):\n    def check(node):\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        l, r = check(node.left), check(node.right)\n        if l < 0 or r < 0 or abs(l - r) > 1:\n            return -1\n        return 1 + max(l, r)\n    return check(root) >= 0","frames":[{"m":"9: heights 0 and 0 → height 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}}]},{"m":"15: heights 0 and 0 → height 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[3],"p":{}}]},{"m":"7: heights 0 and 0 → height 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[4],"p":{}}]},{"m":"20: heights 1 and 1 → height 2","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]},{"m":"3: heights 1 and 2 → height 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"subtree-of-another-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if <code>subRoot</code> appears as a full subtree of <code>root</code>.","examples":[["root = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2], sub = [4, 1, 2]","True"],["root = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2, None, None, None, None, 0], sub = [4, 1, 2]","False"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2], sub = [4, 1, 2]","brute":{"idea":"For every node of root, check whether the tree starting there equals subRoot.","tc":"O(m · n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_subtree(root, sub):\n    def same(a, b):\n        if not a or not b:\n            return a is b\n        return a.val == b.val and same(a.left, b.left) and same(a.right, b.right)\n    if not root:\n        return False\n    return same(root, sub) or is_subtree(root.left, sub) or is_subtree(root.right, sub)"},"opt":{"idea":"Serialise both trees in preorder with markers for None and delimiters around values; subRoot is a subtree exactly when its string is a substring. (Use KMP for a guaranteed linear search.)","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(m + n)","code":"def is_subtree(root, sub):\n    def ser(node, out):\n        if not node:\n            out.append(\"#\")\n            return\n        out.append(f\"^{node.val}\")\n        ser(node.left, out)\n        ser(node.right, out)\n\n    a, b = [], []\n    ser(root, a)\n    ser(sub, b)\n    big, small = \",\".join(a), \",\".join(b)\n    return small in big","frames":[{"m":"Preorder strings with # for None","l":13,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"root","v":[["3",1,4],["4",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"subRoot","v":[["4",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["root","^3,^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#,^5,#,#"],["subRoot","^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#"],["found","T"]]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"root","v":[["3",1,4],["4",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"tree","n":"subRoot","v":[["4",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["2",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["root","^3,^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#,^5,#,#"],["subRoot","^4,^1,#,#,^2,#,#"],["found","T"]]}]}]},"tests":2},"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-search-tree":{"statement":"Return the lowest node in the BST that has both <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> as descendants (a node counts as its own descendant).","examples":[["root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, None, None, 3, 5], p = 2, q = 8","6"],["root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, None, None, 3, 5], p = 2, q = 4","2"],["root = [2, 1], p = 2, q = 1","2"]],"vizIn":"root = [6, 2, 8, 0, 4, 7, 9, None, None, 3, 5], p = 3, q = 5","brute":{"idea":"Use the general binary-tree LCA that ignores the ordering and searches both sides.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def lca_bst(root, p, q):\n    def lca(n):\n        if not n or n.val in (p.val, q.val):\n            return n\n        l, r = lca(n.left), lca(n.right)\n        return n if l and r else l or r\n    return lca(root)"},"opt":{"idea":"Walk from the root: both values smaller → go left; both larger → go right; otherwise this node is where they split — the LCA.","tc":"O(h)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def lca_bst(root, p, q):\n    node = root\n    while node:\n        if p.val < node.val and q.val < node.val:\n            node = node.left\n        elif p.val > node.val and q.val > node.val:\n            node = node.right\n        else:\n            return node","frames":[{"m":"At 6: p = 3, q = 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 2: p = 3, q = 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 4: p = 3, q = 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["6",1,6],["2",2,3],["0",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["3",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["8",7,8],["7",-1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[4,5],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree":{"statement":"Return the lowest common ancestor of nodes <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> in a binary tree (no ordering).","examples":[["root = [3, 5, 1, 6, 2, 0, 8, None, None, 7, 4], p = 5, q = 1","3"],["root = [3, 5, 1, 6, 2, 0, 8, None, None, 7, 4], p = 5, q = 4","5"],["root = [1, 2], p = 1, q = 2","1"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 5, 1, 6, 2, 0, 8, None, None, 7, 4], p = 7, q = 8","brute":{"idea":"Record the root-to-p and root-to-q paths, then take the last node they share.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    def path(n, target, acc):\n        if not n:\n            return False\n        acc.append(n)\n        if n is target or path(n.left, target, acc) or path(n.right, target, acc):\n            return True\n        acc.pop()\n        return False\n    a, b = [], []\n    path(root, p, a)\n    path(root, q, b)\n    i = 0\n    while i < min(len(a), len(b)) and a[i] is b[i]:\n        i += 1\n    return a[i - 1]"},"opt":{"idea":"Each call returns p or q if it finds one below it. The first node that gets a non-empty answer from both sides is the LCA.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    top = root\n\n    def lca(node):\n        if not node or node is p or node is q:\n            return node\n        left, right = lca(node.left), lca(node.right)\n        if left and right:\n            return node\n        return left or right\n    return lca(root)","frames":[{"m":"At 6: left reports None, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 4: left reports None, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 2: left reports 7, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 5: left reports None, right reports 7","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 0: left reports None, right reports None","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[7],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 1: left reports None, right reports 8","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[6],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 3: left reports 7, right reports 8","l":6,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,6],["5",2,3],["6",-1,-1],["2",4,5],["7",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["1",7,8],["0",-1,-1],["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[4,8],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"validate-binary-search-tree":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if the tree is a valid BST (strictly smaller on the left, strictly larger on the right, all the way down).","examples":[["root = [2, 1, 3]","True"],["root = [5, 1, 4, None, None, 3, 6]","False"],["root = [5, 4, 6, None, None, 3, 7]","False"]],"vizIn":"root = [2, 1, 3]","brute":{"idea":"For every node, check that all values in its left subtree are smaller and all in its right are larger.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_valid_bst(root):\n    def vals(n):\n        return [] if not n else vals(n.left) + [n.val] + vals(n.right)\n    if not root:\n        return True\n    if any(v >= root.val for v in vals(root.left)) or any(v <= root.val for v in vals(root.right)):\n        return False\n    return is_valid_bst(root.left) and is_valid_bst(root.right)"},"opt":{"idea":"Pass an allowed (low, high) range down: going left tightens high to the node's value, going right tightens low.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def is_valid_bst(root):\n    def ok(node, low, high):\n        if not node:\n            return True\n        good = low < node.val < high\n        if not good:\n            return False\n        return ok(node.left, low, node.val) and ok(node.right, node.val, high)\n    return ok(root, float(\"-inf\"), float(\"inf\"))","frames":[{"m":"2 must be in (-inf, inf) → OK","l":5,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[0],"p":{}}]},{"m":"1 must be in (-inf, 2) → OK","l":5,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[1],"p":{}}]},{"m":"3 must be in (2, inf) → OK","l":5,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["2",1,2],["1",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3},"kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst":{"statement":"Return the k-th smallest value (1-indexed) in a BST.","examples":[["root = [3, 1, 4, None, 2], k = 1","1"],["root = [5, 3, 6, 2, 4, None, None, 1], k = 3","3"]],"vizIn":"root = [5, 3, 6, 2, 4, None, None, 1], k = 4","brute":{"idea":"Collect the full inorder list and index it.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    def ino(n):\n        return [] if not n else ino(n.left) + [n.val] + ino(n.right)\n    return ino(root)[k - 1]"},"opt":{"idea":"Iterative inorder visits values in sorted order; stop at the k-th pop.","tc":"O(h + k)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    stack, cur, count = [], root, 0\n    while True:\n        while cur:\n            stack.append(cur)\n            cur = cur.left\n        cur = stack.pop()\n        count += 1\n        if count == k:\n            return cur.val\n        cur = cur.right","frames":[{"m":"Inorder visit #1: 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","1"]]}]},{"m":"Inorder visit #2: 2","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","2"]]}]},{"m":"Inorder visit #3: 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","3"]]}]},{"m":"Inorder visit #4: 4","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["5",1,5],["3",2,4],["2",3,-1],["1",-1,-1],["4",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["k","4"],["count","4"]]}]}]},"tests":2},"binary-tree-right-side-view":{"statement":"Return the values visible from the right side, top to bottom.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3, None, 5, None, 4]","[1, 3, 4]"],["root = [1, 2, 3, 4, None, None, None, 5]","[1, 3, 4, 5]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, None, 5, None, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Level-order traversal storing every level, then take each level's last value.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def right_side_view(root):\n    levels, q = [], [root] if root else []\n    while q:\n        levels.append([n.val for n in q])\n        q = [c for n in q for c in (n.left, n.right) if c]\n    return [lv[-1] for lv in levels]"},"opt":{"idea":"DFS visiting right before left; the first node reached at each new depth is the visible one.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def right_side_view(root):\n    res = []\n\n    def dfs(node, depth):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        if depth == len(res):\n            res.append(node.val)\n        dfs(node.right, depth + 1)\n        dfs(node.left, depth + 1)\n\n    dfs(root, 0)\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"First node at depth 0 (coming from the right): 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"First node at depth 1 (coming from the right): 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[0,3],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1","3"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"First node at depth 2 (coming from the right): 4","l":7,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[0,3,4],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 3, 4]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",-1,2],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,4],["4",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[0,3,4],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"view","v":["1","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"construct-binary-tree-from-preorder-and-inorder-traversal":{"statement":"Build the tree from its preorder and inorder traversals (values are unique).","examples":[["preorder = [3, 9, 20, 15, 7], inorder = [9, 3, 15, 20, 7]","[3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]"],["preorder = [-1], inorder = [-1]","[-1]"]],"vizIn":"preorder = [3, 9, 20, 15, 7], inorder = [9, 3, 15, 20, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Take preorder[0] as the root, search for it in inorder to split, and slice lists for each side.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(n²) slices","code":"def build_tree(preorder, inorder):\n    if not preorder:\n        return None\n    root = TreeNode(preorder[0])\n    i = inorder.index(preorder[0])\n    root.left = build_tree(preorder[1:i + 1], inorder[:i])\n    root.right = build_tree(preorder[i + 1:], inorder[i + 1:])\n    return root"},"opt":{"idea":"Same split, but look up the root's inorder index in a dict and recurse on index ranges instead of slices.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def build_tree(preorder, inorder):\n    where = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(inorder)}\n    pre = iter(preorder)\n    holder = {}\n\n    def build(lo, hi):\n        if lo > hi:\n            return None\n        val = next(pre)\n        node = TreeNode(val)\n        holder.setdefault(\"root\", node)\n        node.left = build(lo, where[val] - 1)\n        node.right = build(where[val] + 1, hi)\n        return node\n\n    return build(0, len(inorder) - 1)","frames":[{"m":"Root 3 splits inorder[0..4] at index 1","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4],"ok":[1],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 9 splits inorder[0..0] at index 0","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 20 splits inorder[2..4] at index 3","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[2,3,4],"ok":[3],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 15 splits inorder[2..2] at index 2","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[2],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Root 7 splits inorder[4..4] at index 4","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[4],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["9","3","15","20","7"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[4],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"built so far","v":[["3",1,-1],["9",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":2},"binary-tree-maximum-path-sum":{"statement":"A path goes along parent–child edges and need not pass through the root. Return the largest sum of node values on any non-empty path.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3]","6"],["root = [-10, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","42"],["root = [-3]","-3"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3]","brute":{"idea":"Treat every node as the top of the path and compute the best downward chains from it with separate calls.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def max_path_sum(root):\n    def down(n):\n        return 0 if not n else max(0, n.val + max(down(n.left), down(n.right)))\n\n    def best(n):\n        if not n:\n            return float(\"-inf\")\n        through = n.val + down(n.left) + down(n.right)\n        return max(through, best(n.left), best(n.right))\n    return best(root)"},"opt":{"idea":"Each call returns the best chain going down from the node (dropping negative branches). The path through the node is val + left gain + right gain; keep the max.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def max_path_sum(root):\n    best = float(\"-inf\")\n\n    def gain(node):\n        nonlocal best\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        l = max(gain(node.left), 0)\n        r = max(gain(node.right), 0)\n        best = max(best, node.val + l + r)\n        return node.val + max(l, r)\n\n    gain(root)\n    return best","frames":[{"m":"Path through 2: 2 + 0 + 0 = 2","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","2"],["returns_up","2"]]}]},{"m":"Path through 3: 3 + 0 + 0 = 3","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","3"],["returns_up","3"]]}]},{"m":"Path through 1: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","6"],["returns_up","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 6","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["best","6"],["returns_up","4"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"serialize-and-deserialize-binary-tree":{"statement":"Design <code>serialize(root) → str</code> and <code>deserialize(str) → root</code> so that the tree round-trips exactly.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]","[1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]"],["root = []","[]"],["root = [1, None, 2, None, 3]","[1, None, 2, None, 3]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Store the tree as an array using heap positions (children of i at 2i+1, 2i+2). A skewed tree of n nodes needs about 2ⁿ slots.","tc":"O(2ⁿ) worst","sc":"O(2ⁿ) worst","code":"class Codec:\n    def serialize(self, root):\n        slots = {}\n\n        def put(n, i):\n            if n:\n                slots[i] = n.val\n                put(n.left, 2 * i + 1)\n                put(n.right, 2 * i + 2)\n        put(root, 0)\n        size = max(slots) + 1 if slots else 0\n        return \",\".join(str(slots[i]) if i in slots else \"#\" for i in range(size))\n\n    def deserialize(self, data):\n        if not data:\n            return None\n        vals = data.split(\",\")\n\n        def get(i):\n            if i >= len(vals) or vals[i] == \"#\":\n                return None\n            return TreeNode(int(vals[i]), get(2 * i + 1), get(2 * i + 2))\n        return get(0)"},"opt":{"idea":"Preorder walk writing '#' for every missing child. Reading tokens back in the same order rebuilds the tree, since each '#' tells us where a subtree ends.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"class Codec:\n    def serialize(self, root):\n        out = []\n\n        def dfs(node):\n            if not node:\n                out.append(\"#\")\n                return\n            out.append(str(node.val))\n            dfs(node.left)\n            dfs(node.right)\n        dfs(root)\n        return \",\".join(out)\n\n    def deserialize(self, data):\n        tokens = iter(data.split(\",\"))\n\n        def build():\n            t = next(tokens)\n            if t == \"#\":\n                return None\n            node = TreeNode(int(t))\n            node.left = build()\n            node.right = build()\n            return node\n        root = build()\n        return root","frames":[{"m":"Write 1","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 2","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 3","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2","#","#","3"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 4","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2","#","#","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Write 5","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"tokens","v":["1","2","#","#","3","4","#","#","5"],"p":{},"hl":[8],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Rebuilt by reading the tokens in the same preorder","l":26,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"rebuilt","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["data","1,2,#,#,3,4,#,#,5,#,#"]]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, None, None, 4, 5]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"rebuilt","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",3,4],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["data","1,2,#,#,3,4,#,#,5,#,#"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"binary-tree-zigzag-level-order-traversal":{"statement":"Return the level order traversal, alternating left→right and right→left.","examples":[["root = [3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7]","[[3], [20, 9], [15, 7]]"],["root = [1]","[[1]]"],["root = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Plain level order, then reverse every odd level afterwards.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def zigzag_level_order(root):\n    levels, q = [], [root] if root else []\n    while q:\n        levels.append([n.val for n in q])\n        q = [c for n in q for c in (n.left, n.right) if c]\n    return [lv if i % 2 == 0 else lv[::-1] for i, lv in enumerate(levels)]"},"opt":{"idea":"BFS per level, building each level in a deque: append right on even levels, append left on odd levels.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(w)","code":"def zigzag_level_order(root):\n    from collections import deque\n    if not root:\n        return []\n    res, q, ltr = [], deque([root]), True\n    while q:\n        level = deque()\n        for _ in range(len(q)):\n            node = q.popleft()\n            if ltr:\n                level.append(node.val)\n            else:\n                level.appendleft(node.val)\n            if node.left:\n                q.append(node.left)\n            if node.right:\n                q.append(node.right)\n        res.append(list(level))\n        ltr = not ltr\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Level 0 read left → right: [1]","l":17,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 1 read right → left: [3, 2]","l":17,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[4,1],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1],[3,2]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 2 read left → right: [4, 5, 6, 7]","l":17,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[2,3,5,6],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1],[3,2],[4,5,6,7]]"]]}]},{"m":"Result: [[1], [3, 2], [4, 5, 6, 7]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",5,6],["6",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[2,3,5,6],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["result","[[1],[3,2],[4,5,6,7]]"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"count-good-nodes-in-binary-tree":{"statement":"A node is good if no node on the path from the root to it has a greater value. Count good nodes.","examples":[["root = [3, 1, 4, 3, None, 1, 5]","4"],["root = [3, 3, None, 4, 2]","3"],["root = [1]","1"]],"vizIn":"root = [3, 1, 4, 3, None, 1, 5]","brute":{"idea":"For each node, find its root path again and check the maximum on it.","tc":"O(n · h)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def good_nodes(root):\n    count = 0\n\n    def visit(n, path):\n        nonlocal count\n        if not n:\n            return\n        if all(v <= n.val for v in path):\n            count += 1\n        visit(n.left, path + [n.val])\n        visit(n.right, path + [n.val])\n    visit(root, [])\n    return count"},"opt":{"idea":"DFS passing the largest value seen so far on the path; a node is good if its value ≥ that max.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(h)","code":"def good_nodes(root):\n    good = []\n\n    def dfs(node, high):\n        if not node:\n            return 0\n        is_good = node.val >= high\n        if is_good:\n            good.append(node)\n        high = max(high, node.val)\n        return is_good + dfs(node.left, high) + dfs(node.right, high)\n\n    return dfs(root, root.val)","frames":[{"m":"3 vs path max 3 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","1"]]}]},{"m":"1 vs path max 3 → not good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","1"]]}]},{"m":"3 vs path max 3 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[0,2],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","2"]]}]},{"m":"4 vs path max 3 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[0,2,3],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","3"]]}]},{"m":"1 vs path max 4 → not good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[0,2,3],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","3"]]}]},{"m":"5 vs path max 4 → good","l":9,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[0,2,3,5],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","4"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 4","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,3],["1",2,-1],["3",-1,-1],["4",4,5],["1",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[0,2,3,5],"p":{}},{"k":"vars","v":[["good","4"]]}]}]},"tests":3},"flatten-binary-tree-to-linked-list":{"statement":"Flatten the tree in place into a 'linked list' along right pointers in preorder; all left pointers become None.","examples":[["root = [1, 2, 5, 3, 4, None, 6]","[1, None, 2, None, 3, None, 4, None, 5, None, 6]"],["root = []","[]"],["root = [0]","[0]"]],"vizIn":"root = [1, 2, 5, 3, 4, None, 6]","brute":{"idea":"Record the preorder nodes in a list, then relink them one after another.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def flatten(root):\n    order = []\n\n    def pre(n):\n        if n:\n            order.append(n)\n            pre(n.left)\n            pre(n.right)\n    pre(root)\n    for a, b in zip(order, order[1:]):\n        a.left, a.right = None, b\n    if order:\n        order[-1].left = order[-1].right = None"},"opt":{"idea":"For each node with a left child: find the rightmost node of the left subtree, hang the right subtree there, move the left subtree to the right. Then step right.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def flatten(root):\n    cur = root\n    while cur:\n        if cur.left:\n            tail = cur.left\n            while tail.right:\n                tail = tail.right\n            tail.right = cur.right\n            cur.right, cur.left = cur.left, None\n        cur = cur.right","frames":[{"m":"At 1: hang its right subtree under 4, then move the left subtree to the right","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,1],["2",2,3],["3",-1,-1],["4",-1,4],["5",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[3],"p":{}}]},{"m":"At 2: hang its right subtree under 3, then move the left subtree to the right","l":8,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,1],["2",-1,2],["3",-1,3],["4",-1,4],["5",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Result: [1, None, 2, None, 3, None, 4, None, 5, None, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,1],["2",-1,2],["3",-1,3],["4",-1,4],["5",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2],"p":{}}]}]},"tests":3}},"demo":{"code":"def traversal_demo():\n    root = mk_tree([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, 6])\n    pre, ino, post = [], [], []\n\n    def dfs(node):\n        if not node:\n            return\n        pre.append(node.val)\n        dfs(node.left)\n        ino.append(node.val)\n        dfs(node.right)\n        post.append(node.val)\n\n    dfs(root)\n    return pre, ino, post","frames":[{"m":"Leaving 4: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[2],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 5: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[2,3],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 2: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[2,3,1],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 6: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[2,3,1,5],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5","1","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2","6"],"p":{},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 3: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[2,3,1,5,4],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5","1","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2","6","3"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Leaving 1: it is added to postorder last","l":11,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[2,3,1,5,4,0],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"preorder","v":["1","2","4","5","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"inorder","v":["4","2","5","1","3","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"postorder","v":["4","5","2","6","3","1"],"p":{},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"title":"DFS orders: the same tree visited preorder, inorder, postorder"},"sections":[{"h":"Definition","body":"\n<p>A <b>tree</b> is a <b>non-linear, hierarchical</b> data structure made of nodes connected by edges, with one special node called the <b>root</b> and <b>no cycles</b>. Every node except the root has exactly one parent.</p>\n<p>A <b>binary tree</b> is a tree in which each node has at most two children, called the <b>left child</b> and the <b>right child</b>.</p>\n<p>A <b>binary search tree (BST)</b> is a binary tree where, for every node, all keys in its left subtree are smaller and all keys in its right subtree are larger than the node's key.</p>\n"},{"h":"Terminology","body":"\n<table>\n<tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Root</td><td>top node, no parent</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Parent / child</td><td>a node directly above / below another</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Siblings</td><td>nodes with the same parent</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Leaf (external node)</td><td>node with no children</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Internal node</td><td>node with at least one child</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Edge</td><td>connection between parent and child</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Path</td><td>sequence of nodes connected by edges</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Depth of a node</td><td>number of edges from the root to it (root has depth 0)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Height of a node</td><td>edges on the longest path from it down to a leaf (leaf has height 0)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Height of the tree</td><td>height of the root</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Level</td><td>all nodes at the same depth</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Degree</td><td>number of children of a node</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Subtree</td><td>a node and all its descendants</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Ancestor / descendant</td><td>nodes on the path above / below</td></tr>\n</table>\n"},{"h":"Types of binary trees","body":"\n<table>\n<tr><th>Type</th><th>Definition</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Full (strict)</b></td><td>every node has 0 or 2 children</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Complete</b></td><td>all levels full except possibly the last, which is filled from the left (heaps are complete)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Perfect</b></td><td>all internal nodes have 2 children and all leaves are at the same level</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Balanced</b></td><td>for every node, left and right subtree heights differ by at most 1 (height O(log n))</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Degenerate (skewed)</b></td><td>every node has one child — effectively a linked list (height n − 1)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h4>Self-balancing BSTs</h4>\n<p>Plain BSTs can degenerate to O(n). <b>AVL trees</b> (strict balance by rotations) and <b>Red–Black trees</b> (looser colour rules, used in Java's <code>TreeMap</code> and C++ <code>std::map</code>) keep height O(log n) after every insert and delete. Also: B-trees / B+ trees for databases and file systems, tries for strings, segment trees for range queries.</p>\n"},{"h":"Important properties","body":"\n<ul>\n<li>A tree with <b>n</b> nodes has exactly <b>n − 1</b> edges.</li>\n<li>Maximum nodes at level i (root at level 0): <b>2ⁱ</b>.</li>\n<li>Maximum nodes in a binary tree of height h: <b>2ʰ⁺¹ − 1</b> (a perfect tree).</li>\n<li>Minimum height of a binary tree with n nodes: <b>⌈log₂(n + 1)⌉ − 1</b>.</li>\n<li>In a full binary tree, leaves = internal nodes + 1.</li>\n<li>In a complete binary tree stored in an array, the children of index i are <b>2i + 1</b> and <b>2i + 2</b>, and the parent is <b>(i − 1) // 2</b>.</li>\n<li>Number of structurally different binary trees with n nodes is the Catalan number C(n) = (2n)! / ((n + 1)! n!).</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"h":"Traversals","body":"\n<table>\n<tr><th>Traversal</th><th>Order</th><th>For tree [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</th><th>Uses</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Preorder</b> (DFS)</td><td>Root, Left, Right</td><td>1 2 4 5 3</td><td>copy / serialise a tree, prefix expressions</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Inorder</b> (DFS)</td><td>Left, Root, Right</td><td>4 2 5 1 3</td><td>sorted order of a BST, infix expressions</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Postorder</b> (DFS)</td><td>Left, Right, Root</td><td>4 5 2 3 1</td><td>delete a tree, compute heights/sizes, postfix expressions</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Level order</b> (BFS)</td><td>level by level, left to right</td><td>1 2 3 4 5</td><td>shortest depth, per-level problems</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>All traversals are O(n) time. DFS uses O(h) space (recursion stack); BFS uses O(w) space (widest level). <b>Morris traversal</b> does inorder in O(1) space by temporarily rewiring right pointers.</p>\n<p>A tree can be uniquely rebuilt from <b>inorder + preorder</b> or <b>inorder + postorder</b> (with distinct values), but not from preorder + postorder alone.</p>\n"},{"h":"BST operations and complexity","body":"\n<table>\n<tr><th>Operation</th><th>Balanced BST</th><th>Skewed BST</th><th>How</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Search</td><td>O(log n)</td><td>O(n)</td><td>go left if smaller, right if larger</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Insert</td><td>O(log n)</td><td>O(n)</td><td>search for the spot, attach a new leaf</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Delete</td><td>O(log n)</td><td>O(n)</td><td>leaf: remove; one child: link child to parent; two children: replace with inorder successor (smallest in right subtree), then delete that</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Min / max</td><td>O(log n)</td><td>O(n)</td><td>leftmost / rightmost node</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Inorder (sorted output)</td><td>O(n)</td><td>O(n)</td><td>left, node, right</td></tr>\n</table>\n"},{"h":"Advantages and applications","body":"\n<div class=\"two\">\n<div class=\"pro\"><h5>Advantages</h5><ul><li>Represents hierarchies naturally</li><li>Balanced BSTs: O(log n) search, insert, delete <i>and</i> sorted order</li><li>Range queries, floor/ceiling, k-th smallest</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"con\"><h5>Disadvantages</h5><ul><li>Unbalanced BSTs degrade to O(n)</li><li>Balancing logic (AVL, Red–Black) is complex</li><li>More memory than arrays (two pointers per node)</li></ul></div>\n</div>\n<h4>Applications</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>File systems and folder hierarchies; the HTML DOM; organisation charts.</li>\n<li>Database indexes (B-trees, B+ trees).</li>\n<li>Sorted maps and sets (<code>TreeMap</code>, <code>std::map</code>).</li>\n<li>Expression trees and syntax trees in compilers.</li>\n<li>Decision trees in machine learning; Huffman coding trees in compression.</li>\n<li>Heaps (priority queues) and tries (autocomplete).</li>\n</ul>\n"}],"faq":[{"q":"What's the difference between a binary tree and a BST?","a":"<p>A binary tree only limits each node to two children. A BST adds the ordering rule: left subtree keys &lt; node &lt; right subtree keys, at every node. That rule enables O(h) search.</p>"},{"q":"Depth vs height?","a":"<p>Depth of a node is measured from the root down to the node; height is measured from the node down to its deepest leaf. The root has depth 0; leaves have height 0. The tree's height is the root's height.</p>"},{"q":"Complete vs full vs perfect binary tree?","a":"<p>Full: every node has 0 or 2 children. Complete: all levels filled except possibly the last, which is filled left to right. Perfect: full and all leaves at the same depth (2ʰ⁺¹ − 1 nodes).</p>"},{"q":"Why does inorder traversal of a BST give sorted output?","a":"<p>Inorder visits the left subtree (all smaller keys), then the node, then the right subtree (all larger keys). Applied recursively, every key is output after all smaller keys and before all larger ones.</p>"},{"q":"DFS vs BFS on trees — when to use which?","a":"<p>DFS (recursion) for problems about paths, subtrees and anything computed from children (height, diameter). BFS (queue) for level-based questions (level order, right view, minimum depth). Memory: DFS O(h), BFS O(w).</p>"},{"q":"What is the worst-case time of BST search and how is it avoided?","a":"<p>O(n) when the tree is skewed (e.g., inserting sorted data). Self-balancing trees — AVL or Red–Black — rotate nodes after updates to keep the height O(log n).</p>"},{"q":"How do you delete a node with two children from a BST?","a":"<p>Replace its key with its inorder successor (the minimum of its right subtree) — or predecessor — then delete that successor node, which has at most one child.</p>"},{"q":"Can a tree be rebuilt from its preorder and inorder traversals?","a":"<p>Yes, if keys are distinct: preorder's first element is the root; its position in inorder splits the left and right subtrees; recurse. Preorder + postorder alone is ambiguous when nodes have one child.</p>"}],"lessons":[{"level":"Basics","title":"Tree vocabulary","body":"\n<p>A <b>tree</b> is a set of nodes where each node has one parent (except the <b>root</b>) and any number of children. In a <b>binary tree</b> each node has at most two: <code>left</code> and <code>right</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"pic\">        1          ← root (depth 0)\n       / \\\n      2   3        ← depth 1\n     / \\   \\\n    4   5   6      ← leaves (no children), depth 2       height = 3 levels</div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Leaf</b>: a node with no children.</li>\n<li><b>Depth</b> of a node: edges from the root to it. <b>Height</b> of a tree: number of levels (or edges on the longest root-to-leaf path — check which one the problem means).</li>\n<li><b>Subtree</b>: a node together with everything below it. Every subtree is itself a tree — this is why recursion fits trees so well.</li>\n<li><b>Balanced</b>: height is about log₂ n. A <b>skewed</b> tree is basically a linked list with height n.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>LeetCode writes trees as level-order lists with <code>None</code> for gaps: <code>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, 6]</code>.</p>\n","practice":[],"demo":{"code":"def build_tree_lesson():\n    vals = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, None, 6]\n    root = TreeNode(vals[0])\n    queue, i = [root], 1\n    while queue and i < len(vals):\n        node = queue.pop(0)\n        for side in (\"left\", \"right\"):\n            if i < len(vals) and vals[i] is not None:\n                child = TreeNode(vals[i])\n                setattr(node, side, child)\n                queue.append(child)\n            i += 1\n    return root","frames":[{"m":"Root from vals[0]","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"level-order input","v":["1","2","3","4","5","None","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"vals[1] = 2 becomes the left child of 1","l":11,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"level-order input","v":["1","2","3","4","5","None","6"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,-1],["2",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"vals[2] = 3 becomes the right child of 1","l":11,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"level-order input","v":["1","2","3","4","5","None","6"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[0,1,2],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,2],["2",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"vals[3] = 4 becomes the left child of 2","l":11,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"level-order input","v":["1","2","3","4","5","None","6"],"p":{},"hl":[3],"ok":[0,1,2,3],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,3],["2",2,-1],["4",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"vals[4] = 5 becomes the right child of 2","l":11,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"level-order input","v":["1","2","3","4","5","None","6"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"vals[6] = 6 becomes the right child of 3","l":11,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"level-order input","v":["1","2","3","4","5","None","6"],"p":{},"hl":[6],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"bad":[]},{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["1",1,4],["2",2,3],["4",-1,-1],["5",-1,-1],["3",-1,5],["6",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]}]}},{"level":"Basics","title":"Recursion on trees","body":"\n<p>Nearly every tree solution has the same shape:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">def solve(node):\n    if node is None:          # 1. base case: empty tree\n        return BASE\n    left = solve(node.left)   # 2. trust recursion for the children\n    right = solve(node.right)\n    return combine(node.val, left, right)   # 3. combine</code></pre>\n<p>Example — maximum depth: base is 0, combine is <code>1 + max(left, right)</code>. Count nodes: <code>1 + left + right</code>. Sum: <code>node.val + left + right</code>.</p>\n<h4>The three DFS orders</h4>\n<p>\"Visiting\" a node means doing your work there. Doing it before the children is <b>preorder</b>, between them <b>inorder</b>, after them <b>postorder</b>. Each tree node is visited once → O(n) time, O(h) stack space.</p>\n<div class=\"tip\">Don't trace the whole recursion in your head. Assume the calls on the children return correct answers and only check the combine step and the base case.</div>\n","practice":["binary-tree-inorder-traversal","maximum-depth-of-binary-tree","invert-binary-tree","same-tree","symmetric-tree"]},{"level":"Core","title":"Breadth-first search: level by level","body":"\n<p>DFS dives deep first. <b>BFS</b> visits all nodes at depth 0, then depth 1, then depth 2 … using a <b>queue</b>.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">from collections import deque\nq = deque([root])\nwhile q:\n    level = []\n    for _ in range(len(q)):     # exactly the nodes of this level\n        node = q.popleft()\n        level.append(node.val)\n        if node.left:  q.append(node.left)\n        if node.right: q.append(node.right)\n    print(level)</code></pre>\n<p>The <code>for _ in range(len(q))</code> trick separates levels. Use BFS for anything \"per level\": level order, right side view (last of each level), zigzag, minimum depth (first leaf found).</p>\n","practice":["binary-tree-level-order-traversal","binary-tree-right-side-view","binary-tree-zigzag-level-order-traversal"],"demo":{"code":"def bfs_tree_lesson():\n    from collections import deque\n    root = mk_tree([3, 9, 20, None, None, 15, 7])\n    q, levels = deque([root]), []\n    while q:\n        level = []\n        for _ in range(len(q)):\n            node = q.popleft()\n            level.append(node.val)\n            if node.left:\n                q.append(node.left)\n            if node.right:\n                q.append(node.right)\n        levels.append(level)\n    return levels","frames":[{"m":"Level 0: [3]; the queue now holds the next level","l":13,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["9","20"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["levels","[[3]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 1: [9, 20]; the queue now holds the next level","l":13,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[1,2],"ok":[0],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["15","7"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["levels","[[3],[9,20]]"]]}]},{"m":"Level 2: [15, 7]; the queue now holds the next level","l":13,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"tree","v":[["3",1,2],["9",-1,-1],["20",3,4],["15",-1,-1],["7",-1,-1]],"hl":[3,4],"ok":[0,1,2],"p":{}},{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["levels","[[3],[9,20],[15,7]]"]]}]}]}},{"level":"Core","title":"Bottom-up: return a value, update a global","body":"\n<p>Some answers don't pass through the root. <b>Diameter</b>: the longest path may go through any node. Solve with a postorder DFS that <b>returns</b> one thing (height) and <b>updates</b> another (best answer):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">best = 0\ndef height(node):\n    nonlocal best\n    if not node: return 0\n    l, r = height(node.left), height(node.right)\n    best = max(best, l + r)        # path that bends at this node\n    return 1 + max(l, r)           # what the parent can use</code></pre>\n<p>The same split solves <b>balanced tree</b> (return height or −1) and <b>max path sum</b> (return the best one-sided chain, record the best two-sided path).</p>\n","practice":["diameter-of-binary-tree","balanced-binary-tree","binary-tree-maximum-path-sum"]},{"level":"Core","title":"Top-down: pass information down","body":"\n<p>Sometimes a node needs to know about its <b>ancestors</b>. Pass that info as a parameter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Good nodes</b>: pass the largest value seen on the path from the root.</li>\n<li><b>Validate BST</b>: pass the allowed range <code>(low, high)</code>; going left sets <code>high = node.val</code>, going right sets <code>low = node.val</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Path sums</b>: pass the remaining target.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Bottom-up = \"children tell the parent\". Top-down = \"parent tells the children\". Some problems use both.</p>\n","practice":["count-good-nodes-in-binary-tree","validate-binary-search-tree"]},{"level":"Core","title":"Binary search trees","body":"\n<p>A <b>BST</b> keeps one rule at every node: all values in the left subtree are smaller, all in the right subtree are larger.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Search / insert</b>: compare with the node and go left or right — O(h), which is O(log n) when balanced.</li>\n<li><b>Inorder traversal gives sorted order.</b> So \"k-th smallest\" = the k-th inorder visit; \"validate\" = inorder values strictly increasing.</li>\n<li><b>LCA in a BST</b>: walk from the root; if both targets are smaller go left, if both larger go right, otherwise you're at the split point — the answer.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"warn\">Checking only <code>node.left.val &lt; node.val &lt; node.right.val</code> is not enough — a value deep in the left subtree can still be too big. Use ranges.</div>\n","practice":["lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-search-tree","kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst","validate-binary-search-tree"],"demo":{"code":"def bst_lesson():\n    root = None\n    for v in [8, 3, 10, 1, 6, 14, 4]:\n        if root is None:\n            root = TreeNode(v)\n        else:\n            node = root\n            while True:\n                side = \"left\" if v < node.val else \"right\"\n                nxt = getattr(node, side)\n                if nxt is None:\n                    setattr(node, side, TreeNode(v))\n                    break\n                node = nxt\n    node, path = root, []\n    while node and node.val != 4:\n        path.append(node)\n        node = node.left if 4 < node.val else node.right\n    return root","frames":[{"m":"Insert 8: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",-1,-1]],"hl":[0],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Insert 3: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,-1],["3",-1,-1]],"hl":[1],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Insert 10: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,2],["3",-1,-1],["10",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Insert 1: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,3],["3",2,-1],["1",-1,-1],["10",-1,-1]],"hl":[2],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Insert 6: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,4],["3",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["10",-1,-1]],"hl":[3],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Insert 14: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,4],["3",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["6",-1,-1],["10",-1,5],["14",-1,-1]],"hl":[5],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Insert 4: go left if smaller, right if larger","l":14,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,5],["3",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["6",4,-1],["4",-1,-1],["10",-1,6],["14",-1,-1]],"hl":[4],"ok":[],"p":{}}]},{"m":"Search 4: only one path is checked — O(height)","l":18,"v":[{"k":"tree","n":"BST","v":[["8",1,5],["3",2,3],["1",-1,-1],["6",4,-1],["4",-1,-1],["10",-1,6],["14",-1,-1]],"hl":[0,1,3],"ok":[4],"p":{}}]}]}},{"level":"Advanced","title":"Building, serialising and ancestors","body":"\n<ul>\n<li><b>Build from preorder + inorder</b>: preorder's first value is the root; its position in inorder splits left and right subtrees. A dict of inorder positions makes it O(n).</li>\n<li><b>Serialise</b>: preorder with a marker (<code>#</code>) for every missing child is enough to rebuild the exact tree.</li>\n<li><b>LCA in a general tree</b>: each call returns p or q if found below. The first node that gets an answer from both sides is the LCA.</li>\n<li><b>Flatten / rewire in place</b>: find the rightmost node of the left subtree, hang the right subtree there, move left to right (Morris-style, O(1) space).</li>\n<li><b>Subtree check</b>: serialise both trees and use substring search.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tip\">Python's recursion limit is about 1000. For trees that could be 10⁵ deep, write the DFS with an explicit stack.</div>\n","practice":["construct-binary-tree-from-preorder-and-inorder-traversal","serialize-and-deserialize-binary-tree","lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree","flatten-binary-tree-to-linked-list","subtree-of-another-tree"]}]};
